00:04:09.924 --> 00:04:12.754
that has an amino group on the chains?

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.060
So when we're looking at those
different amino acids, we can organize

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.210
all the different amino acids by
the different properties of it.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.480
So it all starts with hydrophobic,
hydrophilic, So when we're looking

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.030
at all of them, right, we have
20 amino acids that exist, right?

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.280
So 20 essential amino acids that
are essential for your metabolism,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.050
nine of them are hydrophobic.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:42.609
So that includes glycine, alanine, valine,
leucine, isoleucine, phenylalanine,

00:04:42.859 --> 00:04:45.960
methionine, proline, and tryptophan.

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:50.229
Now the hydrophilic ones,
which are water loving, right?

00:04:50.229 --> 00:04:54.530
So because we have that, that love
