00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.469
can be separated based on their pH.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:05:02.920
So if it's acidic, that means that it must
have a carboxylic acid attached to it.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:08.360
So when we have the carboxylic acid
group that's attached to that structure,

00:05:08.879 --> 00:05:13.430
and we're talking about the R group
itself, so where the special feature

00:05:13.439 --> 00:05:18.200
is, then it's going to be acidic because
it has the ability to donate a proton.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:24.220
If it's basic, that must mean that when
we think of basic organic groups, This

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.710
has to have an amine attached to it.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:32.210
Okay, so basic has an amine,
acidic has a carboxylic acid.

00:05:33.094 --> 00:05:34.615
So you're looking for those.

00:05:35.284 --> 00:05:38.664
Now, when it's considered to
be neutral, that's generally

00:05:38.674 --> 00:05:39.924
anything that's just polar.

00:05:39.924 --> 00:05:45.334
So usually anything with alcohols,
amides, uh, are the most common

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:46.865
ones that you're going to be seeing.

00:05:47.254 --> 00:05:49.914
So if you're looking for any of
those different things that usually

00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:54.984
can do hydrogen bonding or dipole
dipole interactions, if you want

00:05:54.984 --> 00:05:56.695
